-- title:
--   Injectivity of substitution along φ with finite kernel algebra
-- statement:
--   Let $B$ be a commutative Noetherian ring and let $\varphi = (\varphi_0,\varphi_1)$ be an element of `Series B`, i.e. a pair of formal power series in $B[[X_0,X_1]]$ (two variables indexed by `Fin 2`), each with vanishing constant coefficient. Assume `FormalODModule.HasKernelOfDegree φ d` holds for some natural number $d$: the kernel algebra $B[[X_0,X_1]]/(\varphi_0,\varphi_1)$, the quotient by the ideal generated by the range of $\varphi$, is a finite $B$-module, is projective as a $B$-module, and for every field $\kappa$ and every ring homomorphism $f \colon B \to \kappa$ the $\kappa$-vector space $\kappa[[X_0,X_1]]/(f(\varphi_0),f(\varphi_1))$, formed from the coefficientwise image of $\varphi$, has dimension $d$. Then, for all $f, g \in B[[X_0,X_1]]$, the equality $f(\varphi_0,\varphi_1) = g(\varphi_0,\varphi_1)$ of substitutions forces $f = g$; that is, the substitution map $\mathrm{subst}\ \varphi$ on $B[[X_0,X_1]]$ is injective.
--
--   This is the algebraic content of the assertion that an isogeny of two-dimensional formal groups is right-cancellable: pre-composition with $\varphi$ is injective on power series, so two homomorphisms of formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-modules that agree after composition with an isogeny agree. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, for instance in the uniqueness statements for homomorphisms composed with the multiplication-by-$p$-power maps of a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module of finite height.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_FormalODModule_subst_injective_of_hasKernelOfDegree.lean

